{
  "k": 3,
  "repository": "cc-enforcer",
  "why": "Grades retrieval on a repository nobody here wrote. The seventy questions in repo_queries.json are asked about this project's own source, by the same party that wrote both the code and its descriptions, on an index where every unit under src/ carries a hand-written bilingual description. That is the warmest case there is, and it cannot see what a first-time user sees: a foreign repository, zero descriptions, ranking decided by nothing but the words the author happened to use.",
  "caveat": "The questions are phrased in a user's words on purpose, not in the words of the docstring that answers them, so a hit means retrieval bridged a paraphrase rather than echoing a string it was handed. Answers were verified one by one against the declarations in the graded repository. The repository itself is external: when it is absent this ruler is skipped, never silently scored as zero.",
